            "n_events": 29,
            "result_text": "Done! I've saved the regex to `/app/regex.txt`. Here's how it works:\n\n**Key components:**\n\n1. **IPv4 lookahead**: `(?=.*\\b(?:25[0-5]|2[0-4]\\d|1\\d{2}|[1-9]?\\d)\\....)` — ensures the line contains a valid IPv4 address with word boundaries (`\\b`) to avoid false matches like \"user192.168.1.1\"\n\n2. **IPv4 pattern** breaks down as:\n   - `25[0-5]` matches 250-255\n   - `2[0-4]\\d` matches 200-249\n   - `1\\d{2}` matches 100-199\n   - `[1-9]?\\d` matches 0-99\n   - No leading zeros allowed\n\n3. **Last date matching**: `.*(?<![A-Za-z0-9])` — greedy matching followed by negative lookbehind ensures we match up to (but not into) the last date\n\n4. **Date validation** with three alternatives:\n   - `\\d{4}-(?:0[13578]|1[02])-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])` — 31-day months (Jan, Mar, May, Jul, Aug, Oct, Dec)\n   - `\\d{4}-(?:0[469]|11)-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\\d|30)` — 30-day months (Apr, Jun, Sep, Nov)\n   - `\\d{4}-02-(?:0[1-9]|1\\d|2[0-9])` — February (01-29)\n\n5. **Boundaries**: `(?<![A-Za-z0-9])` and `(?![A-Za-z0-9])` prevent matching partial alphanumeric sequences\n\nThe regex will correctly extract only the last YYYY-MM-DD date from each line that contains an IPv4 address."
